<main>
<div class="wrap hero">
  <p class="kicker">Documentation</p>
  <h1>Dates without the dread.</h1>
  <p>Sundial is a 4&nbsp;kb JavaScript date library with a humane API: no moment-shaped
  regrets, no 70&nbsp;kb bundle, no "why is February like this" at 2 a.m. Time zones
  handled; daylight saving survived.</p>
  <div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="#install">Install Sundial</a>
  <a class="linklike" href="#api">Skip to the API ↓</a></div>
</div>

<div class="wrap doc">
  <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
    <h4>On this page</h4>
    <a href="#install">Installation</a>
    <a href="#quickstart">Quick start</a>
    <a href="#api">API reference</a>
    <a href="#license">License</a>
  </aside>

  <div class="prose">
    <section id="install">
      <h2>Installation <a class="anchor" href="#install">#</a></h2>
      <p>One package, zero dependencies. Works in the browser, Node, Deno, and Bun —
      anywhere JavaScript runs, Sundial keeps the time.</p>
<pre><span class="c"># npm</span>
npm install sundial-js

<span class="c"># or straight in the browser</span>
&lt;<span class="k">script</span> <span class="k">src</span>=<span class="s">"https://unpkg.com/sundial-js"</span>&gt;&lt;/<span class="k">script</span>&gt;</pre>
      <div class="note"><b>Why 4 kb</b>Most date libraries ship a timezone database the size of a novella. Sundial ships the offsets and computes the rest — the whole thing gzips smaller than most hero images.</div>
    </section>

    <section id="quickstart">
      <h2>Quick start <a class="anchor" href="#quickstart">#</a></h2>
      <p>Everything starts with <code>sun()</code>. It returns an immutable object, so
      every operation gives you a new date and leaves the old one alone.</p>
<pre><span class="k">import</span> { sun } <span class="k">from</span> <span class="s">"sundial-js"</span>;

<span class="k">const</span> <span class="f">launch</span> = <span class="f">sun</span>(<span class="s">"2026-11-02T09:00"</span>, <span class="s">"America/New_York"</span>);
launch.<span class="f">add</span>(<span class="s">"3 days"</span>).<span class="f">format</span>(<span class="s">"EEEE, MMMM d"</span>);
<span class="c">// → "Thursday, November 5"</span></pre>
      <div class="note"><b>Immutable by default</b>If you have ever been bitten by a date that changed itself mid-function, this is the part of the docs where you exhale.</div>
      <h3>Things people ask for first</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Relative time:</b> <code>sun("2026-01-01").fromNow()</code> → "9 months ago"</li>
        <li><b>Calendars:</b> <code>sun().startOf("week")</code> respects locale week starts</li>
        <li><b>Parsing:</b> strict by default — <code>sun("not a date")</code> throws, loudly</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="api">
      <h2>API reference <a class="anchor" href="#api">#</a></h2>
      <p>The complete surface. If a method isn't listed here, it doesn't exist —
      that's a feature.</p>
      <div class="api">
        <div class="api-row"><code class="sig">sun(input?, zone?)</code>
          <p>Creates a Sundial. Accepts ISO strings, <code>Date</code> objects, and Unix timestamps. No arguments means right now, wherever you are.</p></div>
        <div class="api-row"><code class="sig">.add(amount) / .subtract(amount)</code>
          <p>Shifts the date: <code>.add("2 weeks")</code>, <code>.subtract("90 minutes")</code>. Returns a new Sundial; the original is untouched.</p></div>
        <div class="api-row"><code class="sig">.format(pattern)</code>
          <p>Formats with Unicode tokens: <code>"yyyy-MM-dd"</code>, <code>"EEEE, h:mm a"</code>. Unknown tokens throw instead of silently printing themselves.</p></div>
        <div class="api-row"><code class="sig">.inZone(zone)</code>
          <p>Converts to an IANA zone: <code>.inZone("Asia/Tokyo")</code>. DST transitions are handled — spring forward doesn't eat your meeting.</p></div>
        <div class="api-row"><code class="sig">.fromNow() / .calendar()</code>
          <p>Human-friendly output: "in 3 hours", "yesterday". <code>.calendar()</code> gives "Today at 4:30 PM" style strings, localized.</p></div>
        <div class="api-row"><code class="sig">.isBefore(other) / .isAfter(other)</code>
          <p>Comparisons that read like English and behave like math. Granularity optional: <code>.isBefore(other, "day")</code>.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note"><b>Design note</b>Every method returns either a Sundial, a string, or a boolean. If you find yourself nesting three calls deep, file an issue — the API probably owes you a method.</div>
    </section>

    <section id="license">
      <h2>License <a class="anchor" href="#license">#</a></h2>
